# All user state lives under memory/, which is a git
# repository of its own once bin/hostwarden-init has run: the
# workspace of an operations install. It is never part of
# this repository, in solo use or in a team; a team shares it
# through a remote of its own. The templates it starts from
# live in templates/memory/.
memory/

# Project history (auto-maintained by Claude Code).
HISTORY.md

# macOS noise.
.DS_Store

# Claude Code harness runtime artifacts (session/task locks).
# Not shipped with hostwarden; created by /loop, /schedule, and
# the scheduler machinery in the Claude Code CLI.
.claude/*.lock

# Worktrees Claude Code creates for parallel sessions. Only this
# path — the rest of .claude/ is committed agent configuration.
.claude/worktrees/

# Personal Claude Code permission overrides. ALWAYS personal,
# never shared — same category as memory/user.md.
#
# Claude Code appends an allow rule to this file every time you
# approve a command, so it fills up with the literal commands you
# ran, hostnames and all (e.g. an ssh line naming a production
# server). That is exactly the internal detail that must not
# reach a public repo. .claude/settings.json is the shared,
# hostname-free half; this one stays local.
.claude/settings.local.json
